## Bug: `@FeignClient(path=...)` prefix silently overwritten by `@RequestMapping` prefix

When a Feign interface carries **both** `@FeignClient(path="/feign-path")` and `@RequestMapping("/rm-path")`, all three patterns in [`FEIGN_INTERFACE_PREFIX_PATTERNS`](https://github.com/abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus/blob/6c65edad24189aa0e973c3efb51e3ac32a54e14c/gitnexus/src/core/group/extractors/http-patterns/java.ts#L83-L124) will match the same interface node. Because each match calls `.set(interfaceNode.id, prefix)` unconditionally, the last match wins — the `@RequestMapping` prefix (patterns 2 or 3) silently overwrites the `@FeignClient path=` attribute (pattern 1), producing wrong route prefixes for every method in that interface.

**Reproducer:** An interface like:
```java
@FeignClient(name = "svc", path = "/feign-path")
@RequestMapping("/rm-path")
interface MyClient { ... }
```
...would store `"/rm-path"` as the prefix instead of `"/feign-path"`.

**Fix:** Use a "first-wins" guard so the highest-priority pattern (pattern 1 — the explicit Feign `path=` attribute) is never overwritten:

```suggestion
      if (prefix !== null && !feignPrefixByInterfaceId.has(interfaceNode.id)) feignPrefixByInterfaceId.set(interfaceNode.id, prefix);
```

