**Fixed (P1 — query serialization).** Added a **per-handle** FIFO lock (the `conn-lock.ts:30-55` chain mechanic, keyed per cache entry) — deliberately *not* the global `withConnLock`, which would over-serialize every group against the adapter singleton on the hot `@group` path. `queryBridge` runs every conn op on that chain, so two concurrent `@group` callers sharing one cached connection can never dispatch two queries at once. Uncached/writable handles (the `writeBridge` temp DB) are single-threaded and skip the lock at zero cost.

