- closes **exactly once** via a `closeStarted` guard → kills the double-close (incl. the evicted-handle `finally{closeBridgeDb}` you described).

One refinement from a deepening pass on top of your suggestion: the drain must **not** block `writeBridge` on active readers (the lease spans the whole `@group` fan-out, e.g. `cross-impact.ts:598-668`, not just the bridge queries — blocking there would starve `group_sync` unboundedly). So `evictBridgeEntry` awaits the close **only when `refs === 0`** (the common single-threaded `group_sync` — preserving the Windows close-before-rename guarantee); when a reader holds a lease it defers and returns, and `retryRename` covers the rare concurrent-Windows window.

```ts
async function evictBridgeEntry(key, entry) {
  if (!entry.evicted) { entry.evicted = true; if (cachedBridgeHandles.get(key) === entry) cachedBridgeHandles.delete(key); }
  if (entry.refs <= 0) await finalizeBridgeClose(entry);   // refs>0 → deferred to last closeBridgeDb release
